WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
In Chapter 628 of One Piece, we’re&nbsp;
told for the very first time about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:07.980
a mysterious character called Joy Boy.&nbsp;
And over time, he’s turned into maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:13.380
the single most important character&nbsp;
in the entire story next to Luffy

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.240
So let’s dig in to every single thing we know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.380
about Joy Boy for a fact as well as&nbsp;
everything that has been hinted at.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.500
Why do we know only so&nbsp;
little about this character?

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:27.360
Well, not having knowledge about Joy&nbsp;
Boy is actually by design because this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.680
person lived around 800 years ago.&nbsp;
People who know One Piece know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.600
these dates line up perfectly with a&nbsp;
time period called the Void Century.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:43.500
The Void Century is an entire one hundred years&nbsp;
of history that’s just…gone. The World Government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:49.020
the organization that controls the entire&nbsp;
One Piece world, eliminated every shred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:56.100
of information and history connected to&nbsp;
this time period. Almost nothing at all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:03.060
remains. No archaelogoical ruins, no books,&nbsp;
it’s all just vanished with barely a trace.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.020
Except for one big exception,&nbsp;
of course: The Poneglyphs. These&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:13.080
big indestructible blocks are scattered across&nbsp;
the world in a mysterious language. One of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.220
only people in the entire world that knows&nbsp;
how to read the poneglyphs is Nico Robin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.100
the archaeologist of the Straw Hat pirates.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:25.080
And it’s thanks to Robin reading a poneglyph&nbsp;
that we first heard the name Joy Boy in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:29.160
series. While the crew was on Fishman Island,&nbsp;
Robin read a poneglyph there and told us that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:35.280
it described a promise between Joy Boy&nbsp;
and Poseidon from over 800 years ago.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:42.660
Poseidon is one of the ancient weapons and their&nbsp;
power is always reincarnated through the Fishman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:48.420
Royalty of Fishman Island. Whoever holds the&nbsp;
power of Poseidon can command the Sea Kings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.140
gigantic, super powerful sea creatures. Right now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.140
the power of Poseidon belongs to&nbsp;
the Mermaid Princess Shirahoshi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.040
who Luffy saved during the Fishman Island arc&nbsp;
- always leave it to Luffy to save a princess.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:05.160
The promise between Joy Boy and Poseidon 800&nbsp;
years ago had something to do with using the Sea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:12.000
Kings to lift up the massive ark called the Noah&nbsp;
that sits at the bottom of the sea. It probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.320
involves bringing the fishmen to live among the&nbsp;
surface along with the other races of the One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:23.280
Piece world. However, for an unknown reason, Joy&nbsp;
Boy was unable to hold up his side of the deal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:29.460
The poneglyph isn’t actually just a historical&nbsp;
record - it’s an apology to Fishman Island.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:35.760
It was also around this same time that Joy Boy was&nbsp;
also partners with Zunesha - a massive elephant.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:44.280
And I mean MASSIVE - Zunesha is confirmed to be&nbsp;
35 km tall - that means Zunesha is 3 times higher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:52.920
than a Sky Island. Zunesha is SO big in fact, that&nbsp;
a whole island lives on top of him. The minks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:59.820
a race of animal/human hybrids, built their&nbsp;
country Zou right on top of this giant elephant.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:05.460
The crazy thing is that 800 years after&nbsp;
the Void Century, Zunesha is still alive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:11.340
and kicking and has even communicated with&nbsp;
Luffy. Zunesha doesn’t literally talk - he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.200
communicates with other characters through&nbsp;
a mysterious power called the Voice of All&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.660
Things. This power is also supposedly the&nbsp;
way that Roger was able to “read” poneglyphs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:26.640
without knowing how to actually translate the&nbsp;
writing. The thing is though - that entire 800&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.800
years, Zunesha wasn’t freely walking&nbsp;
around the ocean. He was doing time.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:37.140
That’s right - this elephant is a criminal. 800&nbsp;
years ago after committing an unknown crime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:42.300
Zunesha was sentenced to walk a certain&nbsp;
path in the ocean continually for all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.380
that time. It was only once Momonosuke&nbsp;
gave him the order to do something else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:51.180
that he could. For some reason,&nbsp;
Momonosuke, the Shogun of Wano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:57.240
has the power to communicate with Zunesha as well&nbsp;
as even give orders to this gigantic creature.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.280
There are only two more things that are&nbsp;
confirmed pieces of info about Joy Boy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:11.880
First off, Joy Boy is the one who really left&nbsp;
behind the treasure known as One Piece. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.420
series started off with the Pirate King&nbsp;
Gol D. Roger telling the world that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:20.820
left a treasure behind, but the truth is&nbsp;
more complicated than that. In reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:26.520
at the end of his journey, Roger actually found&nbsp;
some kind of object of enormous importance that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:31.680
was left behind by Joy Boy. On this island,&nbsp;
Roger learned the truth of the ancient history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:36.360
and the Void Century and wished that he&nbsp;
could have been alive in Joy Boy’s time.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:42.120
The mysterious treasure that Joy Boy left&nbsp;
behind caused Roger to laugh like crazy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:47.760
leading him to name this island Laugh Tale.&nbsp;
He also revealed that for some reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:54.840
he arrived at Laugh Tale too early.&nbsp;
There goes Oda being mysterious again.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:58.500
We’re not sure why Roger was “too&nbsp;
early” in arriving to Laugh Tale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.400
but it probably has to do&nbsp;
with Joy Boy’s second coming.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:09.060
That’s right - Joy Boy’s coming back. According&nbsp;
to a long-held prophecy, Joy Boy would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:16.380
reincarnated 800 years after the Void Century -&nbsp;
or 20 years after Roger reached Laugh Tale. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:22.200
prophecy is known in part thanks to a character&nbsp;
named Kozuki Oden, the former shogun of Wano&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:29.460
Country. The Kozuki Clan in ancient times were&nbsp;
the ones who actually wrote the poneglyphs. Oden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:36.120
sailed with Gol D. Roger to Laugh Tale and kept a&nbsp;
logbook of their travels. Roger and Oden learned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:39.960
that they’d arrived “too early”, but that in&nbsp;
20 years Joy Boy would return to Wano. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:45.900
led Oden to make his goal of opening Wano’s&nbsp;
borders to welcome Joy Boy in 20 years’ time.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:54.720
And the second Joy Boy…is none other than Monkey&nbsp;
D. Luffy. That’s right - our main character Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:00.840
is the second coming of the legendary hero Joy&nbsp;
Boy. During the fight with the Emperor of the Sea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:07.680
Kaidou, Luffy awakened a new power. What Luffy&nbsp;
calls “Gear 5” is actually the awakening of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.660
devil fruit. After all of these years in the&nbsp;
series, we learned that Luffy’s devil fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:20.160
wasn’t actually the rubber fruit - it was a super&nbsp;
powerful fruit called the Sun God Nika fruit.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:23.880
We still don’t know much about the deity the Sun&nbsp;
God Nika, but we can guess that it’s connected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:30.000
to Joyboy in some way. When Luffy transformed his&nbsp;
hair and clothes turned all white and he couldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:34.320
stop laughing. He also gained new powers this&nbsp;
are seemingly only limited by his imagination.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:38.460
When Luffy first appeared in this new form,&nbsp;
he was also jumping across the battlefield&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:44.220
silhouetted by the moon. This mirrors the very&nbsp;
first time we learned about the Sun God Nika&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:51.360
from Kaidou’s subordinate Who’s Who.&nbsp;
He tells that when he was in prison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:56.820
fellow inmates would tell hopeful tales&nbsp;
of a liberator called the Sun God Nika.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:02.520
During this explanation, we also saw a figure&nbsp;
with a similar silhouette to Gear 5 Luffy.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:06.420
However, when Luffy awakend this form,&nbsp;
Zunesha, the giant elephant said something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:12.660
fascinating. He said he could hear the “drums&nbsp;
of liberation” seemingly referring to Luffy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:18.000
heartbeat. He the announced that “Joy&nbsp;
Boy had returned.” Clearly Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.440
Joy Boy, and Nika are all closely related somehow.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:27.900
It’s ironic that Luffy awakened this form while&nbsp;
fighting with Kaidou because it seemed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:34.980
Kaidou was trying to find Joy Boy or possibly&nbsp;
even trying to become Joy Boy himself. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:41.580
hinted that he might have chosen Wano as his&nbsp;
base because the prophecy hinted that Joy Boy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:47.040
would appear there. Kaidou’s right-hand man,&nbsp;
King, had told him the legends of Joy Boy long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:53.160
ago and Kaidou seemed to become fascinated&nbsp;
with the prophecy and legends of Joy Boy.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:58.440
Kaidou almost defeated Luffy several times&nbsp;
during their battle. After one defeat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:01.140
he dropped Luffy into the sea, stating “So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:06.300
you couldn’t be Joy Boy either.” Clearly&nbsp;
Kaidou had seen others try and fail to fill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:12.600
the role of Joy Boy. It might the case that&nbsp;
Kaidou himself failed at becoming “Joy Boy.”

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:18.600
Even after seeing Kaidou’s flashbacks, much of&nbsp;
his past is mysterious. It would seem that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:23.040
was obsessed with being the strongest, with&nbsp;
creating warfare all across the world. Being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:32.100
the World’s Strongest Creature, it seemed that&nbsp;
his crew followed the rule of “Survival of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.000
Fittest.” However, it seems that another goal&nbsp;
of his was to find Joy Boy all along. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:38.760
part of the prophecy of Joy Boy’s return&nbsp;
involved Wano Country and its borders opening.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:44.760
Wano Country had closed borders for years and&nbsp;
was isolated from the rest of the world. Joy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:50.280
Boy - someone who spreads joy or happiness - and&nbsp;
the Sun God Nika, who represents freedom - as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:56.760
well as the drums of liberation: All of these are&nbsp;
connected in ways we can’t quite see yet. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:01.200
since it’s still such a mystery that gives the&nbsp;
fan base a huge opportunity to make awesome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:07.980
theories about how Joy Boy will play a part&nbsp;
in the story. And if you don’t want to miss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:12.900
any updates on Joy Boy and one piece in general,&nbsp;
you should make sure to subscribe to the channel.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:18.480
But before we talk about speculation, we’ll look&nbsp;
at a likely origin for Joy Boy. Oda might actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:25.920
be drawing on history when creating the idea of&nbsp;
Joy Boy in One Piece. The idea likely comes from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:32.160
Haitian God called…well, Joyboy. In Vodou beliefs,&nbsp;
Joyboy is a God of hope and music. It’s likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:37.980
that Joyboy was originally an African God that was&nbsp;
brought to the Caribbean during the slave trade.

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:44.760
This God is said to spread laughter and joy with&nbsp;
drumming and dancing - which would seem to connect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:50.520
to the idea of the “drums of liberation.”&nbsp;
This God also gave hope to enslaved people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:54.420
which would seem to parallel what we’ve&nbsp;
been told about Sun God Nika in the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:57.900
who is a symbol of hope for&nbsp;
enslaved people in One Piece.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:03.780
And to some fans, it seems like Joy Boy&nbsp;
and his huge significance have come out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:10.440
of nowhere. However, we all know that Oda&nbsp;
is the master of foreshadowing and left us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:15.840
a lot of clues. We already mentioned that Joy&nbsp;
Boy was originally mentioned in a poneglyph&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:21.720
all the way back on Fishman Island, but we’ve&nbsp;
been getting plenty of hints before that, too.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:26.400
In Skypiea, when Luffy was seen silhouetted&nbsp;
in front of a bonfire in a pose that looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:31.980
just like the Sun God Nika. Oda has even said&nbsp;
that it was one of his favorite panels of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:38.880
whole series. In that same arc, the Shandians&nbsp;
worshipped a Sun God. The Giants also worship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.880 --> 00:10:45.360
a Sun God. And the Sun Pirates, who were formed&nbsp;
by former slaves, wear the mark of the Sun - an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:50.460
early hint about slaves praying to the Sun God&nbsp;
Nika for freedom. All of these oppressed people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:56.820
are awaiting the “Dawn of the World” - a Dawn&nbsp;
that can only come with the arrival of the Sun.

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:57.212
Now that we’ve been over all the&nbsp;
things we know for sure about Joy Boy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.212 --> 00:10:59.580
I want to take some time to talk&nbsp;
about the craziest theories about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:04.740
this legendary character. First off - did&nbsp;
the original Joy Boy also wear a Straw Hat?

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:09.960
In a frozen cellar in Mariejois,&nbsp;
the capital of the world government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:17.460
the secret ruler of the world government,&nbsp;
Imu keeps a massive Straw Hat. Why? Did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:23.460
this secret object belong to the first Joy&nbsp;
Boy? And what then is the significance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:28.320
the smaller straw hat that was passed&nbsp;
from Roger to Shanks and then to Luffy?

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:33.480
Also, what did Joy Boy do that was so&nbsp;
significant? We have so little information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:38.880
about him that it’s hard to say what he might&nbsp;
have done. Could he have been the ruler of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:43.560
Ancient Kingdom that went up against the World&nbsp;
Government? The story has recently revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:48.900
the Ancient Kingdom was technologically&nbsp;
advanced - if Joy Boy was its ruler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:54.720
could he have had control over the Ancient&nbsp;
Weapons? Holding that kind of power would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:58.980
enough to make the World Government fearful as&nbsp;
well as jealous. I mean, could Joy Boy have even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:04.920
created the Ancient Weapons…well, if&nbsp;
he’s much like Luffy probably not.

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:09.420
And speaking of that advanced technology that&nbsp;
Dr. Vegapunk has revealed existed in the Ancient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:14.520
Kingdom - what connection does Joy Boy have&nbsp;
to their mysterious power source? Does Joy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:20.700
Boy have something to do with the giant robot that&nbsp;
scaled the Red Line and tried to attack Mariejois&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:25.860
200 years ago? We’ve only just learned about&nbsp;
this powerful weapon of the Ancient Kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:30.300
but it seems pretty convenient that at&nbsp;
the same time it attacked Mariejois,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:36.300
Fishmen were starting to fight for their rights.&nbsp;
Does the mysterious technology of Joy Boy’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:41.820
Ancient Kingdom have something to do with people&nbsp;
fighting for liberation or the coming “dawn”?

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:46.980
Was he the world’s first pirate? Maybe&nbsp;
he was a literal pirate king - not in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:50.700
the sense that Roger was pirate king,&nbsp;
having achieved all a pirate could hope&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:56.940
to achieve. Joy Boy might have been a&nbsp;
the actual ruler of a pirate kingdom.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:02.700
It would make a load of sense then why the&nbsp;
World Government would try to erase his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:08.760
existence. He was their enemy in their war for&nbsp;
supremacy over the One Piece world. In addition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:13.080
if he was a pirate it would make sense that&nbsp;
the World Government would outlaw piracy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:17.460
even against pirates who&nbsp;
don’t steal or harm people.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:23.760
Did he seek a similar dream to Luffy, wanting&nbsp;
to spread freedom and joy wherever he went?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:30.180
Did he unite all the oppressed races of the One&nbsp;
Piece world? If Joy Boy or the Sun God Nika are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:36.240
beacons of hope for enslaved people, perhaps&nbsp;
his dream was to bring people together and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:41.820
prevent discrimination. For instance, the&nbsp;
promise the the Fishmen might have been to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:47.460
use the Noah to bring them to the surface so&nbsp;
that they could live under the sun alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:55.140
humans. Perhaps the minks wouldn’t have to&nbsp;
hide on Zunesha’s back anymore and could also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.140 --> 00:14:01.920
step into the light. Maybe Luffy will be able to&nbsp;
keep the promise that the original Joy Boy broke.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:08.340
And if the original Joy Boy had a giant straw hat&nbsp;
- does that mean that Joy Boy was a giant? And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:13.620
if he lived that long ago…could he have been an&nbsp;
ancient giant? In fact, there’s some pretty strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:18.660
evidence that Joy Boy could be Oars - the giant&nbsp;
zombie that the Warlord Gekko Moriah revived.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:27.900
After all, if Joy Boy had a giant elephant,&nbsp;
shouldn’t he himself be giant, too? And maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:34.740
it was more than a coincidence that Luffy’s shadow&nbsp;
ended up in Oars. But if that’s not convincing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:39.120
then you might just need to check out this video&nbsp;
all about how Joy Boy was an ancient giant!

